2 CONT 10.  '''    HELVIS of Cyprus''' (-after 1 Apr 1324).  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "Marie, Marguerite, Aalis et Helvis" as the four daughters of Hugues III King of Cyprus & his wife[353].  The Chronicle of Amadi records
2 CONC  that "la damisella Chelvis, loro sorella" was present in the royal palace with her brother Amaury Prince of Tyre in 1310[354].  She is named as the king's youngest daughter and unmarried in 1311 by the Aragonese ambassadors[355].
2 CONC   "Helluis de Lisiniaco filia quondam bone memorie domini Hugonis Jerushalem et Cipri regis" wrote to Jaime King of Aragon "cognato eius" dated 26 May [1315/24][356].  She and her sister Alix claimed the throne of Cyprus in 1324, 
2 CONC but the High Court declared in favour of King Hugues IV348. 
