1 TITL Humbert Lord of Meerbeek
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Last son of his father "because of the wars of Cambresis befallen that country" came to Brussels at the age of 15 years. Adult, his business prospered and he acquired the lordship of Meerbeek near Louvain, and was 
2 CONC received as a citizen of Brussels in 1547. The Le Mire had lost their membership of the nobility after their departure from Cambrai but it is the practice of trade that took away their dignity. Peace Women in 1529 did not prevent 
2 CONC the resumption of hostilities between France and Austria (primarily between Francis I and Charles V) and the neutral status of Cambrai was constantly threatened by the presence of soldiers on its territory which caused the ruin of
2 CONC  this region. It should probably located where the departure of Le Mire of Cambrai. Remained at the Old Fish Market-to-which was held at Marche aux herbs present near the Rue des Collines.
