2 CONT TEXT Francois de Bourbon is the son of Louis, Duke of Montpensier and his first wife Jacqueline de Longwy . In 1566, he married Renée d'Anjou , Marquise de Mezieres and Countess de Saint-Fargeau, who was only 16 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT Throughout his life, the prince of the blood of the House of Bourbon accumulates many titles including the dauphin of Auvergne . Until the death of his father in 1582 , it mentions only under the title of "dolphin prince." At the 
2 CONC age of forty, he himself becomes Duke of Montpensier, sovereign prince of Dombes , Sire de Beaujeu and Viscount brush . in 1583, he made Duke of Chatellerault.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the wars of religion , the prince dolphin was given the responsibility of several governments , first in the center of France ( Anjou , Touraine , Maine , Orleans , etc.) and that of the Dauphine in 1567 and finally that of
2 CONC  Normandy in 1588. During the military campaigns, he fights with his father, the Protestants . After the capture of Saint Jean d'Angely , in 1569, he is responsible for fighting in SaintongeBut fails. In 1574, he was appointed gov
2 CONC ernor general of Languedoc and Dauphiné, provinces which are then in the hands of the Protestants.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is naturally of the court of King Henry III of which he became a faithful support. Although zealous Catholic, he refuses to enter into the Holy League headed by the Guise family . When Henry III dies, he supported Henry IV . In
2 CONC  1591, he participated in the siege of Rouen and died the following year. He was buried in the holy chapel Saint-Louis in Champigny-sur-Veude .
