1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fran%C3%A7ois_de_Bourbon,_Count_of_Enghien
2 CONT
2 CONT François de Bourbon, Count of Enghien (23 September 1519 – 23 February 1546) was a French prince of the blood. He was the son of Charles de Bourbon, Duke of Vendôme.
2 CONT
2 CONT Given command of the French army in Italy by Francis I of France during the Italian War of 1542, he was the French commander at the Franco-Ottoman Siege of Nice in 1543, and he led it to victory at the Battle of Ceresole in 1544.
2 CONT
2 CONT His early death at the age of 27 was caused by an accident – falling of a heavy chest – in the castle La Roche-Guyon.
