2 CONT
2 CONT Henri de La Tour d'Auvergne (titular Duke of Bouillon, jure uxoris, comte de Montfort et Negrepelisse, vicomte de Turenne, Castillon, et Lanquais, ) (28 September 1555 – 25 March 1623) was a member of the powerful, (then Huguenot)
2 CONC  House of La Tour d'Auvergne, Prince of Sedan and a marshal of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT The vicomte de Turenne was born at the castle of Joze-en-Auvergne, near Clermont-Ferrand in Auvergne. His parents were François de La Tour d'Auvergne, Viscount of Turenne and Eléonore de Montmorency, eldest daughter of Anne, 1st D
2 CONC uc de Montmorency.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the St. Bartholomew's Day Massacre in 1572 he participated in the Siege of La Rochelle (1572-1573), but subsequently re-converted to Protestantism. Compromised in the conspiracy of La Mole and Coconnat in 1574, he joined the
2 CONC  party of the Malcontents headed by François, Duke of Alençon (younger brother of kings Charles IX and Henry III) in 1575.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1576 he joined the Protestant party of Henry of Navarre (the future Henry IV), negotiating the Peace of Nérac between Protestants and Catholics in 1579. Appointed lieutenant general of Upper Languedoc in 1580, he took part in t
2 CONC he siege of Paris in 1590 after the accession of Henry IV to the throne, and conquered Stenay from the Catholic League in 1591.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1591 Henry IV married him to Charlotte de La Marck, heiress to the duchy of Bouillon (now in Belgium) and of the Principality of Sedan (now in the Ardennes, France). In 1592 Henry IV made him Marshal of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of his wife in 1594, he married Elisabeth of Orange-Nassau, a daughter of William the Silent, by his third wife Charlotte de Bourbon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Defeated at Doullens, Picardy in 1595 by Fuentes, governor of the Spanish Low Countries, he was sent to England to renew the alliance of France with Queen Elizabeth I of England in 1596. Compromised in the conspiracy of Biron in 1
2 CONC 602, he fled to Geneva the following year and had to accept a French protectorate over his duchy of Bouillon in 1606.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the death of Henry IV, he entered the Council of Regency during the minority of Louis XIII, and intrigued against Maximilien de Béthune, duc de Sully and Concini, the latter a favourite of the Queen Regent Marie de' Medici.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Sedan in 1623.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT His only child by Charlotte de La Marck, suo jure Duchess of Bouillon, whom he married on 19 November 1591, was 
2 CONT #son who was born and died on 8 May 1594.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by Elisabeth of Orange-Nassau; married on 15 April 1595:
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue:
2 CONT # Louise de La Tour d'Auvergne (August 1596 – November 1607) died in infancy;
2 CONT # Marie de La Tour d'Auvergne (1601 – 24 May 1665) married Henri de La Trémoille, Duke of Thouars, Prince of Talmont and had issue;
2 CONT # Unnamed son (April 1603)
2 CONT # Juliane Catherine de La Tour d'Auvergne (8 October 1604 – 6 October 1637) married François de La Rochefoucauld, Count of Roucy, Baron of Pierrepont and had issue;
2 CONT # Frédéric Maurice de La Tour d'Auvergne (22 October 1605 – 9 August 1652) married Eleonora Catharina of the Bergh and had issue;
2 CONT # Élisabeth de La Tour d'Auvergne (1606 – 1 December 1685) married Guy Aldonce de Durfort, mother of Jacques and Guy;
2 CONT # Henriette Catherine de La Tour d'Auvergne (1609 - 1677) married Amaury Gouyon, Marquis of La Moussaye, Count of Quintin and had issue;
2 CONT #Charlotte de La Tour d'Auvergne,   d. 29 Jul 1662
2 CONT # Henri de La Tour d'Auvergne, known as the vicomte de Turenne (11 September 1611 – 27 July 1675) married Charlotte de Caumont daughter of Armand Nompar de Caumont; Armand Nompar was the uncle of the scheming Duke of Lauzun.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by Adèle Corret, mistress;
2 CONT #Henri Corret, ancestor of Théophile Corret de La Tour d'Auvergne.
2 CONT
