1 NOTE Grandson of Sigismund I of Poland, for whom he was also named (John 
2 CONT Sigismund). He was elected king shortly after his father's death, while 
2 CONT still in his infancy, but his claim was contested by Ferdinand I of 
2 CONT Germany (later Holy Roman emperor). On the pretext of protecting John's 
2 CONT interests, as he had his father's, the Ottoman sultan Suleiman I, the 
2 CONT Magnificent, then invaded Hungary (1541) and occupied Buda. Ferdinand 
2 CONT finally made peace with Suleiman in 1562, receiving a small part of 
2 CONT Hungary. John's rule was largely confined to Transylvania.
