2 CONT
2 CONT i. NICOLASA5 XIMENEZ-DE-VALDEZ, b. Saltillo, Coahuila, Mexico; m. NICOLAS FLORES-DE-VALDEZ-Y-DUARTE, 03 May 1707, Santiago Apostol, Monclova, Coahuila, Mexico; b. 1680, Saltillo, Coahulia, Mexico; d. 06 Jun 1731, San Antonio, Bexa
2 CONC r County, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for NICOLASA XIMENEZ-DE-VALDEZ: In 1737 she received a land grant from Governor Carlos Benites Franquis de Lugo. Source:San Antonio de Bexar, by Jesus F. de la Teja. Page 35. Notes for NICOLAS FLORES-DE-VALDEZ-Y-DUARTE: Sour
2 CONC ce:Index to the Marriage Investigations of the Diocese of Guadalajara, by Raul J. Guerra., Nadine M. Vasquez, Baldomero Vela, Jr. Page 191. Nicolas Flores de Valdes, who had been Alferez in Monclova in 1693, probably a member of t
2 CONC he Olivares-Espinosa-Aguirre Expedition of 1709. On April 1722, he was appointed Captain of the Presidio as San Antonio de Bexar, being relieved of the command in 1725, was father of Gertrudis, who married Diego Ramon. Source:With
2 CONC  the Makers of San Anonio, by Frederick C. Chabot.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. DOMINGO XIMENEZ-VALDEZ, m. GERTRUDIS NAVARRO.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. MARIA XIMENEZ-VALDEZ, m. CAPTAIN JUAN RODRIGUEZ-RAMOS.
2 CONT
