1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Bernard de Nogaret de La Valette, d'Epernon''' was born on March 18, 1592 in Angoulême, Charente, Poitou-Charentes, France. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-67816531 Jean Louis de Nogaret, duc d'Epernon] and [http
2 CONC s://www.geni.com/profile-67816585 Marguerite de Foix Candale]. He was a Duc d'Epernon and a French General. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard married [https://www.geni.com/profile-26151297 Gabrielle Angelique de Verneuil] on December 12, 1622 in Lyon, Rhône, Rhone-Alpes, France. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-26151375 Lou
2 CONC is Charles de Nogaret de Foix, duc de La Valette et de Candale]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-26151400 Anne-Louise-Christine Louise de Foix de La Valette d'Épernon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard married [https://www.geni.com/profile-68194796 Marie du Cambout] on November 28, 1634 in Paris, Paris, Île-de-France, France. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-64614333 Jean de Nogaret
2 CONC  de La Vallette d'Epernon]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-22570587 Charles D'Epernon]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-36412617 Margaret Nogaret]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on July 25, 1661 in Paris, Île-de-France, France and was buried in July 1661 in Collégiale St Blaise, Cadillac, Gironde, Aquitaine, France. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT *BERNARD DE LA VALLETTE DEFOIX5 NOGARET (*JEAN LOUIS DE NOGARET DE4 LA VALETTE, *JEAN DE LA VALLETTE DE NOGARET3 BARON, *PIERRE NOGARET DE2 LA VALETTE, *BERNARD NOGARET DE1) was born 18 Mar 1592 in Angouleme, Charente, France, and
2 CONC  died 25 Jul 1661 in Paris, France.  He married (1) ANTOINETTE (ANNE) FAUDOAS.  She was born 1597 in Serillac, Gaure, France, and died 1648 in Glamorganshire, Wales.  He married (2) GABRIELLE ANGELIQUE VERNEUIL DE BOURBON 12 Dec 1
2 CONC 622 in Lyons, France, daughter of KING - and MARQUISE DE VERNEUIL.  She was born 21 Jan 1603 in Paris, France, and died 14 Apr 1627 in Metz, France.  He married (3) MARIE DU CAMBOUT 1634 in Paris, France.  She was born 1614 in Fra
2 CONC nce, and died 12 Feb 1691 in Val de Grace, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for *BERNARD DE LA VALLETTE DEFOIX NOGARET:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard de Nogaret de La Valette (1592-1661), duke of Épernon and a French general, was the son of Jean Louis de Nogaret de La Valette and Marguerite de Foix-Candale, grand-daughter of the constable of Montmorency. Through his mot
2 CONC her's line, Bernard could also claim the English title of Duke of Kendal, originally granted to his ancestor John de Foix in 1446.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1622, Bernard married Gabrielle-Angélique de Verneuil, legitimised daughter of Henri IV and the Marquise de Verneuil, with whom he had a son, Louis-Charles-Gaston de Candale, and a daughter, Anne-Louise-Christine de Foix de La 
2 CONC Valette d'Épernon. Gabrielle-Angélique died in 1627 (some say Bernard poisoned her) and in 1634 he married Marie Ducambaut, a niece of Cardinal Richelieu. It was not a happy marriage, as Bernard later conceived a life-long passion
2 CONC  for a middle-class woman named Ninon de Lartigue, who exerted absolute power over him and to whom he gave enormous sums of money.
2 CONT
2 CONT Like his father, Bernard made a career of the military. He was named Colonel-General of infantry and fought at the sieges of Saint-Jean-d'Angély and of Royan (1621) and at the attack of the pas de Suse (1629). On 15 May 1633, Bern
2 CONC ard became a Chevalier du Saint-Esprit and in 1635 he was charged by Louis XIII with restoring the order which had been disturbed by lifting of taxes and religious passions. He fought in Picardy (1636), in Guyenne, and finally aga
2 CONC inst the Spaniards, and repressed the Peasants' Revolt (Révolte des Croquants) in 1637.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Fled France when Cardinal Richelieu accused him of complicity with the enemy (Huguenots) at the battle of Fontarable (1636) ; first fled to the Netherlands then to Glamorganshire, Wales. Executed in effigy on 6/6/1639. Returned to
2 CONC  France in 1643 and was rehabilitated, and lived in his estate Louches where he died
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/h/e/n/Elaine-Hensley/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0096.html 
2 CONT
2 CONT Entry on Wikipedia
2 CONT
2 CONT CURATOR NOTE:  One reason is that their marriage was given at the same date as Nogaret's wedding date with Marie du Cambout (and he couldn't have married twice on the same day. Secondly, there is not indication of any third marria
2 CONC ge of Nogaret. Nogaret fled to England in 1638 (to escape unwarranted persecution for war acts), and came back to France in 1643 (and justice was done to him by the courts). In between those years, he became a colonel of the so-ca
2 CONC lled "Bandes françaises" in 1641. He later inherited the dukedom. Besides his two known marriages, he had a life-long relationshop with Ninon de Lartigue, with whom he may have fathered children. '''However, there is no trace of a
2 CONC ny relationship of https://www.geni.com/people/Bernard-de-Nogaret-de-La-Valette-d-Epernon/6000000000883831185 to an Antoinete de Faudoas, nor of any offspring that emigrated to America.'''
