2 CONT
2 CONT Louis XIII, Roi de France was born on 27 September 1601 at Fontainebleau, Île-de-France, France. (4) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Henri IV, Roi de France and Marie de Medici. (1), (4) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Ana Maria Maurica von Habsburg, Princesa de España, daughter of Felipe III von Habsburg, Rey de España and Margarete Erzherzogin von Österreich, on 24 November 1615 at Bordeaux, Dauphine, France. (4) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 14 May 1643 at age 41 at Saint-Germain-en-Laye, Île-de-France, France. (4) He was buried at Saint-Denis, Île-de-France, France. (4) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis XIII, Roi de France also went by the nick-name of Louis 'le Juste' (?). (4) He was a member of the House of Bourbon. (1) He was styled as Dauphin de France between 1601 and 1610. (4) He succeeded to the title of Roi Louis XI
2 CONC II de France on 14 May 1610. (1) He was crowned King of France and Navarre on 17 October 1610 at Rheims, Champagne, France. (4) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Louis XIII, Roi de France and Ana Maria Maurica von Habsburg, Princesa de España 
