1 NOTE Also called Casimir V.  He became a Roman Catholic cardinal in 1640. When 
2 CONT his older brother King Wladyslaw IV Vasa of Poland died, John was elected 
2 CONT to succeed him. His reign was marked by the invasions of Tatars and 
2 CONT cossacks (1649), a disastrous 13-year war with Russia (1654-1667), and a 
2 CONT war with Sweden (1655-1660). After abdicating in 1668, John retired to an 
2 CONT abbey in Nevers, France.
