2 CONT
2 CONT Mademoiselle de Chartres Marie Anne d'Orléans House -	House of Orléans Father -	Gaston d'Orléans Mother -	Marguerite de Lorraine Born - 	9 November 1652, Palais d'Orléans, Paris, France Died -	17 August 1656 (aged 3), Palais d'Orl
2 CONC éans, Paris, France Burial -	Royal Basilica of Saint Denis
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Anne d'Orléans, petite-fille de France (Marie Anne; 9 November 1652 – 17 August 1656) was a French Princess and youngest daughter of Gaston d'Orléans. She held the rank of Grand daughter of France. She was a member of the Ho
2 CONC use of Orléans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at the Palais d'Orléans,[1] the present day Luxembourg Palace in Paris, she was the youngest daughter born to the Duke and Duchess of Orléans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father, Gaston d'Orléans, was the youngest brother of the late Louis XIII; as such, Marie Anne was born during the reign of his first cousin, the 12 year old Louis XIV. As a grand daughter of France, Marie Anne was allowed the
2 CONC  style of Royal Highness and was known as Mademoiselle de Chartres from birth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her older siblings included the future Grande Mademoiselle,[2] the Grand Duchess of Tuscany, Duchess of Guise and the short lived Duchess of Savoy. Her only brother the Duke of Valois died in 1652 aged a year and a half.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died at the Palais d'Orléans and was buried at the '''Royal Basilica of Saint Denis''' outside Paris, the traditional burial place of the House of Bourbon.
