1 OCCU 9th Earl of Derby
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William George Richard Stanley, 9th Earl of Derby1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #13890, b. 18 March 1656, d. 5 November 1702
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=25 Oct 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT      William George Richard Stanley, 9th Earl of Derby was born on 18 March 1656.2 He was the son of Charles Stanley, 8th Earl of Derby and Dorothea Helena van den Kerchhove.2 He married Lady Elizabeth Butler, daughter of Thomas B
2 CONC utler, Earl of Ossory and Lady Amelia de Nassau, on 10 July 1673.2 He died on 5 November 1702 at age 46, without surviving male issue.2
2 CONT
2 CONT      William George Richard Stanley, 9th Earl of Derby held the office of Sovereign Lord of the Isle of Man.2 He succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Strange [E., 1628] on 21 December 1672.2 He succeeded to the title of 9th Earl of 
2 CONC Derby [E., 1485] on 21 December 1672.2 He held the office of Vice-Admiral of Lancashire and Cheshire between 1673 and 1702.2 He held the office of Lord-Lieutenant of Cheshire between 1676 and 1689.2 He held the office of Lord-Lieu
2 CONC tenant of Lancashire between 1676 and 1689.2 He held the office of Chamberlain of Chester between 1677 and 1702.2 He held the office of Lord-Lieutenant of North Wales in 1702, except Denbighshire.2 He held the office of Lord-Lieut
2 CONC enant of Lancashire between June 1702 and November 1702.2 On his death, the Barony of Strange fell into abeyance between daughters.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William George Richard Stanley, 9th Earl of Derby and Lady Elizabeth Butler
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Stanley d. 23 Apr 1714
2 CONT
2 CONT James Stanley, Lord Strange2 b. 28 Jun 1680
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrietta Maria Stanley, Baroness Strange+1 b. c 1687, d. 26 Jun 1718
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct 
2 CONC or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 135. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1102. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peer
2 CONC age and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Stanley, 9th Earl of Derby
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT William Richard George Stanley, 9th Earl of Derby (c. 1655 – 5 November 1702), known as Lord Strange from 1655 to 1672, was an English peer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Derby was the eldest son of Charles Stanley, 8th Earl of Derby, and Dorotha Helena Kirkhoven. He succeeded his father in the earldom in 1672 and later served as Lord Lieutenant of Lancashire from 1676 to 1687 and again from 1688 t
2 CONC o 1701 and of Cheshire from 1676 to 1687. Lord Derby married Lady Elizabeth Butler, daughter of Thomas Butler, Earl of Ossory, in 1673. His only son James Stanley, Lord Strange, predeceased him. On his death in November 1702 his j
2 CONC unior title of Baron Strange fell into abeyance between his two daughters (it was later called out abeyance in favour of the eldest daughter, Henrietta). He was succeeded in the earldom by his younger brother James Stanley, 10th E
2 CONC arl of Derby. Lady Derby died in 1717.
