2 CONT (119) '''William Murray''', fourth son of John (No. 101), born c. 1665; died 3rd February 1726. He married, February 1690, Margaret, only daughter and heiress of Robert, first Lord Nairne (title created 1681), and he then became s
2 CONC econd Lord NAIRNE under the special remainder of the title. He sided with the Jacobites in 17 15, was taken prisoner, and condemned to death, but was pardoned, his title being however forfeited. On 24th June 172 1 he had a Jacobit
2 CONC e Peerage conferred on him - EARL OF  Nairne and Viscount Stanley. His widow died 14th November 1747, 
