2 CONT
2 CONT Louis Auguste de Bourbon, Duc du Maine et d'Aumâle was born illegitimately on 31 March 1670 at Saint-Germain-en-Laye, Île-de-France, France. (3) He was the son of Louis XIV, Roi de France and Françoise Athénaïs de Rochechouart. (1
2 CONC ) He married Anne Louise Bénédicte de Bourbon, daughter of Henri Jules de Bourbon, Prince de Condé and Anne Henriette Julie Pfalzgräfin von Simmern, on 19 March 1692 at Versailles, Île-de-France, France. (3) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 14 May 1736 at age 66 at Château de Sceaux, France. (3)
2 CONT
2 CONT      Louis Auguste de Bourbon, Duc du Maine et d'Aumâle gained the title of Comte d'Eu. (1) He gained the title of Duc d'Aumâle. (1) He gained the title of Duc de Maine. (1) In December 1674 his birth was legitimised. (3)
2 CONT
