2 CONT Anne Marie Louise d'Orléans, Duchess of Montpensier, (27 May 1627 – 5 April 1693) known as La Grande Mademoiselle, was the eldest daughter of Gaston d'Orléans, and his first wife Marie de Bourbon, Duchess of Montpensier. One of th
2 CONC e greatest heiresses in history, she died unmarried and childless, leaving her vast fortune to her cousin, Philippe of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mademoiselle caught smallpox, but survived the illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_Marie_Louise_d'Orl%C3%A9ans,_Duchess_of_Montpensier
