1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Charles Beauclerk, 1st Duke of St Albans, KG (8 May 1670 – 10 May 1726) was an illegitimate son of King Charles II of England by his mistress Nell Gwynne."
2 CONT
2 CONT =============================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://www.thepeerage.com/p10504.htm#i105034 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/U/per_page.php?id=80661 Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Beauclerk,_1st_Duke_of_St_Albans Wikipedia]
2 CONT *[http://www.findagrave.com//memorial/15117027/charles-beauclerk]
2 CONT *[http://histfam.familysearch.org/getperson.php?personID=I54065&tree=Nixon Family Search]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10838-8291313/charles-beauclerk-in-genealogieonline-family-tree-index GenealogieOnline Family Tree Index] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 
2 CONC 22 2021, 23:40:07 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://berkshirehistory.com/bios/cbeauclerk_1dofsa.html
2 CONT * https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Charles_Beauclerk,_1st_Duke_of_St_Albans
2 CONT * https://www.britannica.com/biography/Charles-Beauclerk-1st-duke-of-Saint-Albans
2 CONT * https://dayhist.com/persons/charles-beauclerk-1st-duke-st-albans
2 CONT * https://1066.co.nz/Mosaic%20DVD/whoswho/text/Charles_Beauclerk_1st_Duke_of_St_Albans[1].htm
2 CONT * https://artsandculture.google.com/asset/charles-beauclerk-1670%E2%80%931726-duke-of-st-albans-0006/lgE1FltfLFdUSg
2 CONT * https://monarchy-of-the-united-kingdom.fandom.com/wiki/Charles_Beauclerk,_1st_Duke_of_St_Albans
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles, 1st Duke of St. Albans was born in Lincoln's Inn Fields, Westminster, Middlesex, England and passed away in Bath, Somersetshire, England. He was the illegitimate son of King Charles II and his mistress Eleanor (Nell) Gwyn
2 CONC ne. He married Lady Diana de Vere, the daughter of Aubrey de Vere, 20th Earl of Oxford and Diana Kirkie, on April 13, 1694. The couple had twelve children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon his mother's death, on 14th November 1687, Beauclerk received a considerable estate, the chief property of which was Burford House, adjoining Windsor Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1688, he served in the Holy Roman Imperial army against the Turks, and was present at the taking of Belgrade on 20th August of that year. The Duke took his place in the House of Lords on 9th November 1691. On 17th May 1693, he 
2 CONC left for Flanders and served under William III in the campaign of Landen.
2 CONT
2 CONT In April 1694, the Duke married Lady Diana de Vere, daughter and sole heiress of Aubrey de Vere, the 20th and last Earl of Oxford. He served in Flanders as a volunteer in the July following and, the next month, received a pension 
2 CONC of £2,000 a year from the Crown. In 1718, was made a Knight of the Garter.
