3 TEXT Prince Rupert was Duke of Cumberland and Earl of Holderness in the English peerage. He never married, but left two illegitimate children: his mistress Frances Bard bore him a son, Dudley Bard, in 1666; his second mistress, the act
4 CONC ress Peg Hughes, bore him a daughter, Ruperta, in 1673. Rupert's sister, Sophia, Electress of Hanover, was the mother of George I, the first Hanoverian King of Great Britain.
