1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LIST OF NAMES OF PARENTS & SPOUSES OF THE ORIGINAL GRANTEES
2 CONT
2 CONT Investigation of the mineral estate status on Spanish and Mexican land grants in South Texas reveals that many appear to have royalties going into suspense, or have in the past had royalties going into suspense. Production Reports
2 CONC  as of April, 2010 indicate that some part of the mineral estate remains in the unknown heirs on the following grants:
2 CONT *Original Grantee Jacinto de la Pena
2 CONT *Spouse / Spouses Francisca Benavides
2 CONT *Parents Jacinto de la Pena Sr. and Ana Maria Guajardo
2 CONT *Notes Porcion 25, Zapata County
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.eileenmckenziefowler.com/Spousal-And-Parental-Grantees.cfm
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From Spanish and Mexican Land Grants of South Texas by the Villa De San Agustin - Laredo Genealogy Society:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.vsalgs.org/stnemgenealogy/grants.html
2 CONT
2 CONT De La Peña, Jacinto
2 CONT *Porcion 25 , Guerrero (Granted: 1767)
2 CONT *6876 acres located in Zapata County 
2 CONT *Next Owner: Treviño, Rafael (Heirs)
