0 @N6000000002322320733@ NOTE He was the last of the direct line of Jagiellon kings, who united Livonia and
1 CONT the duchy of Lithuania with Poland, creating a greatly expanded legally
1 CONT unified kingdom. The Livoronian War with Czar Ivan IV the Terrible had
1 CONT compelled Sigismund to strengthen his position by constitutionally uniting
1 CONT all the lands attached to the Polish crown. Supported by the Polish and
1 CONT Lithuanian gentry, Sigismund ceded his heretitary rights in Lithuania to
1 CONT Poland in 1564, thus placing the two states in constitutional equality.
