1 CONT (proxy) Kronborg 20 Aug 1589, (in person) Oslo 23 November 1589 and again
1 CONT Kronborg 21 Jan 1590. James convoked the Hampton Court Conference (1604) at
1 CONT which he authorized a new translation of the Bible, genreally called the King
1 CONT James Version.  aka: James VI of Scotland.
0 @N6000000002322325809@ NOTE In 1582, at the age of 15, James became responsible for the Government in
1 CONT Scotland. In 1603, James found accession to the crown of England, thereby
1 CONT creating a union of crowns when Queen Elizabeth I of England died on March
1 CONT 24, 1603. She was the last of her line, having had no children, as well as her
1 CONT own legitimacy questioned by the rules of the Church with respect to divorce.
1 CONT 1st James King of Great Britain, 1603-1625, King of Scotland, 1567-1625.
