1 CONT Hisgrand palace at Versailles afforded the ideal setting for his lavish court.
1 CONT Louis razed the city's medieval walls, built the Invalides as a home for
1 CONT disabled veterans, planned the great avenue of the Champs-Elysees, and
1 CONT refurbished the Cathedral of Notre Dame.  His personal example of long,
1 CONT dedicated rule made France the bureaucratic model for 18th century, absolutist
1 CONT Europe.  His first wife, Marie-Therese, was his double first cousin.
