1 CONT [edit] Marriage and Issue
1 CONT Painting of Charles I's children. The future Charles II is depicted at centre, stroking the dog
1 CONT Painting of Charles I's children. The future Charles II is depicted at centre, stroking the dog
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles was father to a total of nine legitimate children, two of whom would eventually succeed him as king. Several other children died in childhood.[41]
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles is also believed to have had a daughter, prior to his marriage with Henrietta Maria. Her name was Joanna Brydges, born 1619-20, the daughter of a Miss Brydges ("a member of a younger branch of the ancient Kentish family of
1 CONC  that name"), possibly from the line of Brydges of Chandos and Sudeley. Joanna Brydges who was provided for by the estate of Mandinam, Carmarthenshire, was brought up in secrecy at Glamorgan, Wales. She went on to become second wi
1 CONC fe to Bishop Jeremy Taylor, author of Holy Living and Holy Dying and chaplain to both Archbishop Laud and Charles I. The Bishop and his wife Joanna Brydges left for Ireland, where Jeremy Taylor became Bishop of Down, Connor and Dr
1 CONC omore in 1660. Joanna Brydges and Jeremy Taylor had several children, including two daughters, Joanna Taylor(Harrison) and Mary Taylor (Marsh).[42][43][44]
1 CONT
